\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Non-uniqueness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Different subsurface models can produce similar responses.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Equivalence\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Different combinations of layer properties may produce similar electrical responses.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Geological ambiguity\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The same resistivity range may correspond to different materials under different conditions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 1D assumptions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Real geology may vary laterally.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Data quality\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Bad measurements can distort interpretation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Overinterpretation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 A mathematically good model should not automatically be presented as geological certainty.\
These limitations need to be part of the scientific design.\
